<title>USA: Fed stays out of banking system during usual time.</title>
<headline>Fed stays out of banking system during usual time.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve remained out of the banking system during its usual midmorning intervention period on Friday.</p>
<p>The lack of action was not unexpected, though some economists saw the possibility of weekend systems to add reserves.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-3/8 percent, slightly below the Fed's current official target level of 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>(( N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
